cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "AKS: C++ implementation of the Lenstra variant of the AKS primality test"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Renders
    given-names: Vincent J.
    email: vince@render3d.tech
repository-code: "https://github.com/render3d/AKS"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Two C++ implementations of the Lenstra (2002) variant of the
  Agrawal-Kayal-Saxena deterministic primality test: a Zn[x] version using
  NTL's polynomial arithmetic and a Z version using binary segmentation
  (Kronecker substitution). Written for a 2021 University of Bath MSc
  dissertation and corrected in 2026 (tag v1.1).
keywords:
  - AKS
  - primality testing
  - number theory
  - binary segmentation
  - NTL
